WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:02.470
Three phones, one break time.

2
00:00:03.060 --> 00:00:07.240
A lock code of one-two-three-four, a game

3
00:00:07.240 --> 00:00:10.460
that wants to read messages, and a phone

4
00:00:10.460 --> 00:00:13.080
left on a bus — with no backup.

5
00:00:13.750 --> 00:00:14.250
Right.

6
00:00:15.040 --> 00:00:15.860
Let’s fix this.

7
00:00:17.140 --> 00:00:20.320
Today: six quick settings that lock down

8
00:00:20.320 --> 00:00:22.500
your phone — and everything on it.

9
00:00:23.640 --> 00:00:26.080
Your phone holds your email, mobile

10
00:00:26.080 --> 00:00:28.800
money, photos and parents’ numbers.

11
00:00:29.570 --> 00:00:32.010
If someone gets in, they get all of that.

12
00:00:32.630 --> 00:00:34.470
So start with the screen lock.

13
00:00:35.160 --> 00:00:37.940
Codes like one-two-three-four or your

14
00:00:37.940 --> 00:00:39.580
birth year are guessed first.

15
00:00:40.300 --> 00:00:42.220
Choose six digits or more,

16
00:00:42.540 --> 00:00:43.660
with no link to you.

17
00:00:44.860 --> 00:00:45.960
Next, updates.

18
00:00:46.760 --> 00:00:49.280
Many fix security holes criminals could

19
00:00:49.280 --> 00:00:52.180
use — so don’t keep tapping “later”.

20
00:00:52.690 --> 00:00:53.430
Low on data?

21
00:00:54.150 --> 00:00:56.270
Update on Wi-Fi or with a bundle.

22
00:00:56.940 --> 00:00:59.020
And install apps only from your

23
00:00:59.020 --> 00:01:01.600
phone’s official store — never from

24
00:01:01.600 --> 00:01:03.200
a file or link in a chat.

25
00:01:04.430 --> 00:01:07.370
Then check app permissions — what each

26
00:01:07.370 --> 00:01:09.430
app is allowed to use: camera,

27
00:01:09.910 --> 00:01:13.250
microphone, contacts, location, messages.

28
00:01:14.060 --> 00:01:16.840
Ask one question: does this app

29
00:01:16.840 --> 00:01:18.460
need that to do its job?

30
00:01:19.650 --> 00:01:21.070
A map needs your location.

31
00:01:21.900 --> 00:01:24.360
A torch app doesn’t need your contacts.

32
00:01:25.220 --> 00:01:27.520
If the answer is no, switch the

33
00:01:27.520 --> 00:01:29.900
permission off — or delete the app.

34
00:01:31.120 --> 00:01:31.520
Quick check!

35
00:01:32.140 --> 00:01:33.620
My new torch app wants to

36
00:01:33.620 --> 00:01:34.360
read my messages.

37
00:01:35.160 --> 00:01:36.760
That’s fine, isn’t it?

38
00:01:37.930 --> 00:01:38.170
No.

39
00:01:38.740 --> 00:01:41.220
A torch doesn’t need your messages.

40
00:01:42.090 --> 00:01:45.110
Switch that permission off, or delete the

41
00:01:45.110 --> 00:01:47.490
app and use the phone’s own torch.

42
00:01:48.610 --> 00:01:51.170
Now get ready for a lost phone.

43
00:01:51.890 --> 00:01:54.110
Check that “find my device” is on

44
00:01:54.110 --> 00:01:56.230
today — you can’t switch it on

45
00:01:56.230 --> 00:01:57.310
once the phone is gone.

46
00:01:58.000 --> 00:02:00.140
Then, from another phone, you can

47
00:02:00.140 --> 00:02:02.540
ring it, lock it or erase it.

48
00:02:03.690 --> 00:02:06.450
And back up your photos and contacts — to

49
00:02:06.450 --> 00:02:08.510
your online account or a computer.

50
00:02:09.230 --> 00:02:09.970
Low on data?

51
00:02:10.690 --> 00:02:12.970
Let backups run on Wi-Fi only.

52
00:02:13.590 --> 00:02:15.810
Then a lost phone is a bad

53
00:02:15.810 --> 00:02:17.290
day, not a disaster.

54
00:02:18.780 --> 00:02:19.540
Your turn.

55
00:02:20.160 --> 00:02:22.840
A colleague’s lock code is her birth year.

56
00:02:23.390 --> 00:02:24.690
What’s the best advice?

57
00:02:26.170 --> 00:02:28.630
Six digits with no link to her.

58
00:02:29.240 --> 00:02:31.240
Remember the check-up: a strong

59
00:02:31.240 --> 00:02:33.920
lock, updates, apps from the

60
00:02:33.920 --> 00:02:35.860
official store, sensible

61
00:02:35.860 --> 00:02:39.380
permissions, find my device, and a backup.

62
00:02:40.680 --> 00:02:43.080
Try it in class tomorrow: draw a

63
00:02:43.080 --> 00:02:44.240
big phone on the board.

64
00:02:44.880 --> 00:02:47.980
In pairs, pupils role-play a phone clinic

65
00:02:47.980 --> 00:02:50.820
— one brings a problem card, the other

66
00:02:50.820 --> 00:02:52.780
picks the fix and explains why.
